---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Smash repair services | Stewart & Armstrong"
  description="Explore body repairs, paint and refinishing, and repair assessment at Stewart and Armstrong."
  activePath="/services.html"
>
  <div class="page-heading container">
    <h1>
      Repairs, from panel
      <br />
      to paint.
    </h1>
    <p>Tell us what needs attention. We’ll talk through the work with you.</p>
  </div>
  <section class="service-detail container" id="body-repairs">
    <div class="detail-photo">
      <img
        src="/images/bodywork.jpg"
        alt="A masked rear body panel ready for paintwork"
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
    </div>
    <div class="detail-copy">
      <h2>Body repairs.</h2>
      <p>
        For damaged bodywork and panels that need attention. The starting point
        is a closer look at the affected area and the work involved.
      </p>
      <ul class="plain-list">
        <li>Damaged panels and bodywork</li>
        <li>Panel preparation before refinishing</li>
        <li>Repair scope discussed after assessment</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="inline-link" href="/contact.html">
        Discuss body repairs
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="service-detail container reverse" id="paint">
    <div class="detail-photo">
      <img
        src="/images/paint.jpg"
        alt="Red paint samples compared with the vehicle paint finish"
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </div>
    <div class="detail-copy">
      <h2>Paint &amp; refinishing.</h2>
      <p>
        Preparation, colour and finish are part of the same job. The work begins
        with the surface and continues through to the final appearance.
      </p>
      <ul class="plain-list">
        <li>Surface preparation and masking</li>
        <li>Paint colour comparison</li>
        <li>Refinishing the repair area</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="inline-link" href="/contact.html">
        Discuss paintwork
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="service-detail container" id="assessment">
    <div class="detail-photo">
      <img
        src="/images/workshop.jpg"
        alt="Vehicles inside our Chatswood repair workshop"
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </div>
    <div class="detail-copy">
      <h2>Repair assessment.</h2>
      <p>
        Not sure what your car needs? Start by explaining what happened. An
        assessment helps establish the repair scope before arrangements are
        made.
      </p>
      <ul class="plain-list">
        <li>Describe the damage and how it happened</li>
        <li>Have your vehicle make and model ready</li>
        <li>Discuss the next steps with the team</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="inline-link" href="/contact.html">
        Contact the workshop
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section soft-section">
    <div class="container faq-layout">
      <h2>Before you start.</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <details>
          <summary>What information should I have ready?</summary>
          <p>
            Your vehicle’s make and model, a brief description of the damage and
            any relevant photographs are useful starting points.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can you confirm a price from a photograph?</summary>
          <p>
            A photograph may help explain the damage, but repair scope and cost
            need to be confirmed with the workshop after assessment.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How long will the repair take?</summary>
          <p>
            Timing depends on the work required and any parts needed. Ask the
            team about availability and an estimated timeframe for your vehicle.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container end-cta">
      <h2>Let’s talk about your repair.</h2>
      <a class="button" href="/contact.html">
        Contact us
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
